{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And now, strip your ornaments from upon you.</b> It is surprising, for it was already said: ולא שתו איש עדיו עליו. And one may answer: they did not intend to remove them permanently but only temporarily, and they thought to return them afterward. Therefore it says: הורד עדיך — not as you think, but strip them completely, and do not return to putting them back. And R. Yosef Kara, of blessed memory, explained: ולא שתו איש עדיו עליו — these are desirable and beautiful garments that they wore at the time of the giving of the Torah, as it is written: ויכבסו שמלותם. But הורד עדיך — these are the crowns that were given to them at the moment they said נעשה ונשמע, and the angels of destruction stripped them when they served the calf, as is concluded in tractate Shabbat. And this is what it says: ויתנצלו בני ישראל — the angels of destruction took them, and it is not written וינצלו. Another explanation: ולא שתו — [they did not put on] weapons, for they said: we shall not go to battle, but only when the Holy One, blessed be He, goes with us. And He said: הורד עדיך עד שאדע מה אעשה לך — for I shall go with you."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:34.535642765Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}